## Section 6: Recommendations & Next Steps {#section-6-recommendations-next-steps}

### Priority 1: Critical Fixes (Before Any Production Deployment) {#priority-1-critical-fixes-before-any-production-deployment}

1. **Fix rate limiter to fail closed in production** (Section 1.2)
2. **Add middleware for API route protection** (Section 1.3)
3. **Fix refresh token cookie path** (Section 1.5)
4. **Implement logout revocation & audit logging** (Section 1.6)
5. **Verify TOTP UI form logic** (Section 1.4)

**Estimated effort:** 4\-6 hours\
**Testing:** Full auth flow test suite required

### Priority 2: High\-Priority Fixes (Before Scaling to 15k DAU) {#priority-2-high-priority-fixes-before-scaling-to-15k-dau}

1. Fix in\-memory rate limiter memory leak (Section 2.1)
2. Implement password expiration policy (Section 2.4)
3. Add request ID for distributed tracing (Section 2.2)
4. Improve TOTP migration logic (Section 2.3)

**Estimated effort:** 8\-10 hours

### Priority 3: Medium\-Priority Enhancements {#priority-3-medium-priority-enhancements}

1. Add CORS middleware (Section 3.2)
2. Fix timing attack on email enumeration (Section 3.1)
3. Add rate limiting to password change route (Section 3.3)
4. Add API documentation (OpenAPI/Swagger)

**Estimated effort:** 6\-8 hours

### Priority 4: Long\-Term (Scaling Phase) {#priority-4-long-term-scaling-phase}

1. Implement database\-level RLS
2. Add structured logging (ELK/Datadog)
3. Add integration/e2e tests
4. Implement health check endpoint
5. Add metrics/observability dashboard

