## Section 7: Security Testing Recommendations {#section-7-security-testing-recommendations}

### Manual Testing Checklist {#manual-testing-checklist}

- [ ] Test login with correct credentials
- [ ] Test login with incorrect credentials (should lock after 5 attempts)
- [ ] Test TOTP 2FA flow
- [ ] Test backup codes
- [ ] Test session refresh
- [ ] Test logout revocation (try to use old refresh token)
- [ ] Test CSRF protection (submit form from different origin)
- [ ] Test rate limiting (10 login attempts from same IP in 15 min)
- [ ] Test permission checks (Finance Admin accessing Teacher Admin routes)
- [ ] Test audit logging (verify all sensitive actions are logged)

### Automated Testing {#automated-testing}

```bash
# Run existing tests
npm run test
npm run test:coverage

# Run security tests (if available)
npm run test:security

# Run linting and security linter
npm run lint
npm run scan:sast
npm run scan:secrets
```

* * *

## Conclusion {#conclusion}

The admin panel is **well\-designed and professionally built**, but it **must not be deployed to production** without fixing the 6 critical issues detailed in Section 1. The architecture is sound, and with these fixes, it will be production\-ready.

**Timeline to production readiness:** 1\-2 weeks (depending on test coverage)

**Sign\-off required from:** Security team, Backend lead, QA lead

